  "description": "QOSKAN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H82 Gd9 N24 O42 1+,N1 O3 1-,3(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.323-5.507 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 80.54-168.53°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd9(C8H9N2O)8(μ3-OH)8(μ4-OH)2(NO3)8](NO3)·5CH3OH·3H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
